<BaseLayout title="Privacy | ZeroSend" description="How ZeroSend keeps supported file processing local to your browser and separates file data from website services.">
  <section class="section"><div class="container narrow"><p class="eyebrow">PRIVACY</p><h1>Your selected files stay out of our processing servers.</h1><p>ZeroSend is designed so the supported tools in this site perform their file operations in your browser. The processing implementation must not transmit selected-file bytes, content, filenames, previews, extracted text, or generated output to our servers or third parties.</p><h2>What can still use the network?</h2><p>The website itself needs network access to load pages and assets. In later releases, consent management, analytics, or advertising may also make ordinary requests. Those systems are kept separate from file-processing state and must not receive file-derived information.</p><h2>Temporary browser memory</h2><p>Your browser can keep file data in memory while a task runs. ZeroSend does not intentionally persist your selected files in a ZeroSend account or cloud database because the MVP has neither.</p><h2>Third-party services</h2><p>When production advertising or measurement is introduced, this page will identify the providers and applicable consent controls before those systems are enabled.</p><h2>Verify the behavior</h2><p>Advanced users can inspect their browser's developer tools Network panel while selecting and processing a file. Tool processing should not produce a request carrying the selected file or derived file content.</p><h2>Contact and updates</h2><p>This policy will be updated when production hosting, analytics, consent, or advertising configuration changes. The repository documents the engineering boundary used to preserve local processing.</p></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
